# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and must stay that way.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# The Postgres DATABASE password (Supabase dashboard → Project Settings →
# Database → Database password). Not the service-role key above, and not your
# Supabase account password.
#
# Required by `pnpm db:push`, which loads .env.local automatically — you do NOT
# need to export it in your shell. If it is missing, db:push stops with an
# explicit message naming this variable rather than prompting or half-running.
#
# `pnpm db:types` does NOT need it: --project-id goes through the Management API
# and authenticates with your `supabase login` session instead.
#
# KEEP THE DOUBLE QUOTES. Node's .env parser treats an unquoted # as the start of
# a comment, so a generated password containing one is silently truncated and you
# get a confusing auth failure rather than a parse error.
SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=""

RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=

NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Cloudflare R2 — public asset storage (tool cover thumbnails). Server-only.
# These are ORDINARY secrets and may live in Vercel: they only grant write to a
# bucket of PUBLIC images and cannot decrypt anything (unlike ENCRYPTION_KEY,
# below, which must never be on Vercel). See lib/r2.ts.
#   R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL — the bucket's public URL (r2.dev or a custom domain),
#                        no trailing slash, e.g. https://pub-xxxx.r2.dev
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Shared secret proving "our backend sent this" to the run-tool Edge Function.
# Set the SAME value in Supabase secrets (supabase secrets set RUNNER_SECRET=...)
# AND here / in Vercel (server-only). It cannot decrypt anything — ENCRYPTION_KEY
# is not on Vercel — so it does not weaken the §13 property.
RUNNER_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Creem — the payment provider. The only one: Paddle is retired, and its route,
# its signature helper and its client SDK are deleted rather than left dormant.
#
# NOTE the deliberate interim state: CREEM_TEST_MODE is true, so checkout runs
# against Creem's sandbox and NO REAL MONEY IS COLLECTED. Going live is one env
# flip plus a live product id in plans.provider_price_id — see the note below.
#
# Server-only, both of them. Neither may ever gain a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix:
# CREEM_API_KEY creates checkout sessions and CREEM_WEBHOOK_SECRET is what
# proves a webhook is genuine — in the browser bundle, either is a spend/forge
# primitive.
CREEM_API_KEY=
CREEM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Test vs live, env-driven so it is never hardcoded. Defaults to TEST when
# unset: the failure mode of a missing var should be sandbox money, not real
# money. Set to exactly "false" to go live.
CREEM_TEST_MODE=true

# NOTE: there is no CREEM_PRODUCT_ID. The product the Subscribe button checks out
# is DATA, not config — plans.provider_price_id on the slug='member' row, read by
# lib/billing.ts. Moving test→live or switching product is one UPDATE and no
# redeploy, which is the whole reason it lives there.

# NOTE: there is no CREEM_WEBHOOK_IPS. Creem's docs state they "do not provide
# static source IP addresses for outbound webhooks in either Test Mode or
# production" and direct you to verify the signature instead. The webhook route
# is signature-only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENCRYPTION_KEY IS DELIBERATELY NOT IN THIS FILE. NOBODY FORGOT IT.
#
# It encrypts members' API keys, and it lives in Supabase secrets and nowhere
# else — not here, not in .env.local, and above all NOT IN VERCEL. The only code
# that reads it is supabase/functions/_shared/crypto.ts, which only ever runs on
# Supabase.
#
# That absence is what lets us say: a total compromise of the Vercel project
# yields ciphertext and nothing else. Adding it here would quietly destroy the
# security property in CLAUDE.md §13.
#
# Set it once, at setup, and back it up:
#     supabase secrets set ENCRYPTION_KEY="$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
#
# If you lose it, every member's stored API key is permanently unrecoverable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
